<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gaia (Numidian king)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died c. 207 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gaia, also called Gala, was king of the Massylii, the eastern Numidian people of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a>, in the late third century BCE and the father of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/masinissa">Masinissa</a>. An ally of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a>, he sent his son to fight for the Carthaginians in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-punic-war">Second Punic War</a>. After his death around 207 BCE the throne passed to his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oezalces">Oezalces</a>, and a civil war followed.</p></div>
